<section class="band" id="mission">
  <div class="band__inner">
    <p class="label">What we believe</p>
    <p class="statement">The loops you learned early run your love life, your friendships and your work. <em>Change one, and you feel it everywhere.</em></p>
    <hr class="rule">
    <p class="lede">Our mission is to help you build the skills to relate and connect with the people in your life more effectively, wherever you are in the country.</p>
    <p class="soft">We imagine a world full of people who can stay close through the hard moments, in love, with friends, at work and in their communities, and an earth that gets to be a better, healthier playground for all of us.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<main id="main" class="reading">
  <div class="reading__inner">
    <section class="section" id="values">
      <p class="label">What you can count on</p>
      <h2>Our <em>values</em></h2>
      <hr class="rule">
      <ul class="values-list">
        <li><strong>Connection</strong><span>People heal and grow in relationship. We gather in person whenever we can.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Compassion in action</strong><span>We look closely, and we’re kind and honest about what we see.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Curiosity</strong><span>Feelings carry information and instructions. We get curious about what they’re telling us.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Discernment and choice</strong><span>Good judgment can be learned. Every choice is yours, and each one teaches you something.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Practice</strong><span>Love is an action. Like any skill, it can be practiced, tested and improved.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Coherence</strong><span>Who you are inside and how you show up can match. We help you show up authentically and resourcefully, wherever you are.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Open-minded rigor</strong><span>We consider the source, and we stay open to ideas others have dismissed.</span></li>
      </ul>
      <p class="soft">You’re the scientist of your own life, and we bring the tools and the room. Nothing about you needs fixing. What gets shared in the room stays there.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</main>

<section class="band" id="story">
  <div class="band__inner">
    <p class="label">Why this exists</p>
    <h2>Practice, <em>not just insight</em></h2>
    <hr class="rule">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>JD Carlston comes from a family of engineers and teachers. She spent more than twenty years leading engineering teams, and even longer hosting gatherings and peer support in her community. Both taught her the same thing: people rarely change because they understand something. They change when they get to practice it, safely, with honest feedback, until it holds.</p>
      <p>Red Thread Labs is that practice, built for how we love, befriend and work together. The red thread is the pattern you carry from room to room. Once you can see it, you can choose differently.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band--alt" id="people">
  <div class="band__inner">
    <p class="label">Who you’ll work with</p>
    <h2>Built it. <em>Live it.</em> Teach it.</h2>
    <hr class="rule">
    <div class="about">
      <img src="{{ 'img/photo-stairway.jpg' | media }}" alt="JD Carlston and Chick Adams" loading="lazy">
      <div class="prose">
        <p><strong>JD Carlston</strong> is a Human Engineer and the founder of Red Thread Labs. She turned two decades of engineering rigor on the patterns that shape how we love. <a href="/about/jd/">Read JD’s story →</a></p>
        <p><strong>Chick Adams</strong> is co-founder, a DevOps engineer, and JD’s husband. They did this work on themselves first, and still do. We practice before we teach.</p>
        <p>Behind them is a small network of coaches and facilitators we trust, so you get the right person for what you’re working on.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

